#: codec/1/238/0xee440/20
msgid ""
"He says we're born with no defined nature,\n"
msgstr ""
"他说我们生来没有既定本性，\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/21
msgid ""
"and that we're free to make our \"self\" what we wish.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以自由塑造想要的\"自我\"。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/22
msgid ""
"Free? So he was one of those devil-may-care kind\n"
"of guys, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"自由？所以他也是那种天不怕地不怕的\n"
"家伙？\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/23
msgid ""
"No, actually he meant that because we are free to\n"
"create our own life,\n"
msgstr ""
"不，其实他的意思是，正因我们能自由\n"
"创造人生，\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/24
msgid ""
"we must take full responsibility for our actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"就必须为自己的行为负全责。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/25
msgid ""
"\"Man is condemned to be free,\" is how he put it.\n"
msgstr ""
"\"人被判处自由\"，他是这么说的。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/26
msgid ""
"Condemned to be free...\n"
msgstr ""
"被判处自由...\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/27
msgid ""
"But then others will take it upon themselves to\n"
"define who you are.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那样一来，别人就会擅自\n"
"定义你是谁。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/28
msgid ""
"I've been feeling that way lately.\n"
msgstr ""
"我最近就有这种感觉。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/29
msgid ""
"I keep telling people to call me \"Snake,\" but nobody\n"
"seems to listen.\n"
msgstr ""
"我一直让人叫我“斯内克”，可似乎\n"
"没人肯听。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/30
msgid ""
"Sartre also says, \"Hell is other people.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"萨特还说过，\"他人即地狱\"。\n"

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/31
msgid ""
"Hell... Well we are outside of Heaven.\n"
msgstr ""
"地狱...我们可是在天堂外。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 445..1170
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/0
msgid ""
"Do you have an interest in the visual arts, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，你对美术感兴趣吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 1198..2340
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/1
msgid ""
"Not really. Please, no deep conversation...\n"
msgstr ""
"不太感兴趣。别聊太深奥的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 2368..2953
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/2
msgid ""
"But you have heard of Picasso, yes?\n"
msgstr ""
"但你总听说过毕加索吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 2995..3566
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've heard the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，听过这名字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4555
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/4
msgid ""
"Sadly, Monsieur Picasso, co-founder of cubism,\n"
msgstr ""
"可惜，立体主义的创始人毕加索先生，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 4555..5377
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/5
msgid ""
"passed away in the south of France last year.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6297
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/6
msgid ""
"France was his home, you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 6311..7105
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/7
msgid ""
"Huh? I thought he was born in Spain...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7592
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/8
msgid ""
"Do you know his full name?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 7634..8749
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/9
msgid ""
"Pablo Picasso. Anyone would know he's Spanish\n"
"with a name like...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 8749..9264
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/10
msgid ""
"Hmph. Shows what you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 9626..10184
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/12
msgid ""
"OK, here we go.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11870
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/13
msgid ""
"Pablo Diego José Francisco de Paula Juan\n"
"Nepomuceno María de los Remedios...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 11870..12942
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/14
msgid ""
"...Cipriano de la Santísima Trinidad Ruiz y Picasso.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 13318..14113
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/15
msgid ""
"What do you think? That was his full name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 14140..14823
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/16
msgid ""
"Still, I don't see how...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 14823..16453
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/17
msgid ""
"A master of modern art. A genius who crafted over\n"
"100,000 works in various styles,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 16453..17972
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/18
msgid ""
"spending the greater part of his life in France. The\n"
"man is a part of our culture.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19407
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/19
msgid ""
"Yeah that kind of stuff is of limited use in my field...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 19476..20967
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/20
msgid ""
"But back to the point - Picasso was Spanish,\n"
"right? Or am I missing something?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 21385..22346
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/21
msgid ""
"He wasn't French, right? Right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 22945..23280
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/22
msgid ""
"Cécile?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 23447..23976
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/23
msgid ""
"What difference does it make?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 23976..24910
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/24
msgid ""
"It doesn't matter if he was from Spain or from\n"
"Mars,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 24952..26345
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/25
msgid ""
"Picasso is Picasso. It does not change the fact\n"
"that he lived in France,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 26387..27264
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/26
msgid ""
"nor does it take away from his monumental legacy!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 27320..28072
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/27
msgid ""
"Why do you care so much about where he was\n"
"from, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 28128..29493
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/28
msgid ""
"Whatever happened to the \"Sans Frontières\" part\n"
"of \"Militaires Sans Frontières\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 29744..30859
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/29
msgid ""
"You started it. \"France was his...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 30873..31207
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/30
msgid ""
"What was that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0180_000_0
#. timeline 31235..31583
#: codec/1/238/0xeee70/31
msgid ""
"...Nothing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/0
msgid ""
"Tell me, Snake, do you ever put sweets in your\n"
"rations?\n"
msgstr ""
"斯内克，你会在\n"
"口粮里放甜食吗？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/1
msgid ""
"Never thought about it before. Why?\n"
msgstr ""
"从没想过。怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/2
msgid ""
"I simply love them! French sweets are très délicieux.\n"
msgstr ""
"我就是爱甜食！法国的甜点非常美味。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/3
msgid ""
"Everyone knows crêpes, but there are also\n"
"profiteroles,\n"
msgstr ""
"人人都知道可丽饼，但其实还有\n"
"泡芙，\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/4
msgid ""
"éclairs, madeleines, financiers...\n"
msgstr ""
"泡芙、玛德琳、费南雪...\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/5
msgid ""
"Then there's Tarte Tatins, and you can't forget\n"
"savarins.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后是挞挞，还有你不能忘记的\n"
"萨瓦兰。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/6
msgid ""
"Oh, and mille-feuilles, crêpes, blancmanges...\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，还有千层酥、可丽饼、牛奶冻……\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/7
msgid ""
"You already mentioned crêpes.\n"
msgstr ""
"可丽饼说过了。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/8
msgid ""
"Soufflés, croquembouches, canelés, floretins, kouign\n"
"amanns, Peach Melbas...\n"
msgstr ""
"舒芙蕾、焦糖泡芙塔、可露丽、弗洛雷坦、库因\n"
"阿曼、桃子梅尔巴……\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/9
msgid ""
"Finished?\n"
msgstr ""
"说完了吗？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/10
msgid ""
"...And macarons! I love those the most.\n"
msgstr ""
"……还有马卡龙！我最爱那个了。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/11
msgid ""
"Macarons parisiens are the best.They're so cute\n"
"and colorful,\n"
msgstr ""
"巴黎马卡龙最棒了。又可爱\n"
"又五彩缤纷，\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/12
msgid ""
"and they contain meringue, so they melt right in\n"
"your mouth.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且含蛋白霜，会在\n"
"你嘴里融化。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/13
msgid ""
"Wow. I'd no idea macaroons were that popular in\n"
"France, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"哇。我都不知道马卡龙在法国也\n"
"这么受欢迎。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/14
msgid ""
"What do you mean \"in France, too\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"“在法国也”啥意思？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/15
msgid ""
"Macaroons are those coconut-flavored cookies,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"马卡龙就是那种椰子味饼干，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/16
msgid ""
"Excuse you! Macarons contains almond powder, not\n"
"coconuts!\n"
msgstr ""
"拜托！马卡龙里是杏仁粉，不是\n"
"椰子！\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/17
msgid ""
"Don't they have peanuts in them? I've had them in\n"
"Japan a few times.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面不是花生吗？我在日本\n"
"吃过几次。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/18
msgid ""
"I thought they were called \"makorons.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为那叫“马卡隆”。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/19
msgid ""
"Makarons? Some cheap imitation, I am sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"马卡隆？肯定是廉价仿制品。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/20
msgid ""
"French macarons have a long and distinguished\n"
"history.\n"
msgstr ""
"法国马卡龙有着悠久而卓越的\n"
"历史。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/21
msgid ""
"They date back to the 16th century, when\n"
"Catherine de' Medici of Florence\n"
msgstr ""
"可以追溯到16世纪，佛罗伦萨的\n"
"凯瑟琳·德·美第奇\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/22
msgid ""
"married into the French royal family.\n"
msgstr ""
"嫁入法国王室的时候。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/23
msgid ""
"The story goes that her pâtissiers shared the\n"
"recipe after they arrived.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说她的糕点师到来后\n"
"分享了配方。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/24
msgid ""
"That's a history of over 500 years.\n"
msgstr ""
"那可是500多年的历史。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/25
msgid ""
"So... they're originally from Italy, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以……它其实源自意大利。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/26
msgid ""
"Well...\n"
msgstr ""
"这个嘛……\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/27
msgid ""
"Don't macaroons come from Italy, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"马卡龙不也来自意大利吗？\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/28
msgid ""
"Look, I do not really think...\n"
msgstr ""
"我说，我真不觉得……\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/29
msgid ""
"Keep in mind \"macaron\" is almost identical to\n"
"\"macaroni.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"记住，“马卡龙”和“通心粉”\n"
"几乎一模一样。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/30
msgid ""
"Well, that settles it.\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧，就这样。\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/31
msgid ""
"...I cannot believe this. To associate macarons with\n"
"macaroni!\n"
msgstr ""
"……我真不敢相信。竟然把马卡龙和\n"
"通心粉联系在一起！\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/32
msgid ""
"You, Monsieur Miller, are an insensible oaf!\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒先生，你真是个蠢货！\n"

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/33
msgid ""
"Hey, hey, why am I the bad guy? Come on, Cécile,\n"
"wait! Cécile!\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，嘿，为什么我是坏人？拜托，塞西尔，\n"
"等等！塞西尔！\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/0
msgid ""
"Hello! Snake, mon chéri.\n"
msgstr ""
"你好！SNAKE，亲爱的。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/1
msgid ""
"You been drinking, Cécile?\n"
msgstr ""
"塞西尔，你喝酒了？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/2
msgid ""
"Can't you please do something about this pest?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能不能管管这个烦人的家伙？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/3
msgid ""
"Who?\n"
msgstr ""
"谁？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/4
msgid ""
"Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒先生。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/5
msgid ""
"What's he done now...\n"
msgstr ""
"他又干什么了……\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/6
msgid ""
"Wine.\n"
msgstr ""
"葡萄酒。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/7
msgid ""
"Wine?\n"
msgstr ""
"葡萄酒？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/8
msgid ""
"He said he thought the soldiers might tire of\n"
"having beer all the time,\n"
msgstr ""
"他说他觉得士兵们可能会厌倦\n"
"一直喝啤酒，\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/9
msgid ""
"so he's brought in some wine instead. And then he\n"
"gave me a bunch.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以他带了葡萄酒来。然后他\n"
"给了我一大堆。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/10
msgid ""
"That was... nice of him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他……还挺好心。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/11
msgid ""
"But the past two years have been bad for French\n"
"wine.\n"
msgstr ""
"但过去两年对法国\n"
"葡萄酒来说很糟糕。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/12
msgid ""
"Perhaps it is the bad weather we have had, but\n"
"whatever the case,\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是天气不好，但\n"
"不管怎样，\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/13
msgid ""
"I told him the last thing you want to be drinking\n"
"right now is French wine.\n"
msgstr ""
"我告诉他，你现在最不想喝的\n"
"就是法国葡萄酒。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/14
msgid ""
"California and Chile have good wine, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"加州和智利的酒也不错。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/15
msgid ""
"But then he goes and stocks the pantry with\n"
"nothing but French wine from '72.\n"
msgstr ""
"但后来他却在食品储藏室里\n"
"只放满了72年的法国葡萄酒。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/16
msgid ""
"The stuff is a disaster.\n"
msgstr ""
"那玩意儿简直是灾难。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/17
msgid ""
"Then he says, \"Come on, Cécile, have a taste of\n"
"the old country.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"然后他说：“来吧，塞西尔，尝尝\n"
"故乡的味道。”\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/18
msgid ""
"I had a terrible feeling about it, so I decided to just\n"
"taste it at first.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有一种不祥的预感，所以我决定先\n"
"尝一口。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/19
msgid ""
"And then again, and then a few more times.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后又一口，再几口。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/20
msgid ""
"Took one for the team, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"替大家试毒了？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/21
msgid ""
"But when you do a tasting, don't you usually spit\n"
"the wine out?\n"
msgstr ""
"但品酒的时候，一般不都是\n"
"把酒吐出来吗？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/22
msgid ""
"But bottle after bottle, nothing but garbage,\n"
"absolute garbage.\n"
msgstr ""
"可一瓶接一瓶，全是垃圾，\n"
"彻头彻尾的垃圾。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/23
msgid ""
"Not one half-decent bottle in the whole lot! \"Taste\n"
"of the old country\" he says...\n"
msgstr ""
"一整批里连一瓶像样的都没有！他居然说\n"
"\"有故乡的味道\"……\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/24
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""
"真遗憾。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/25
msgid ""
"I cannot believe this! What will we do with all this\n"
"wine!\n"
msgstr ""
"我真不敢相信！这么多酒\n"
"可怎么办啊！\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/26
msgid ""
"The guys aren't too picky when it comes to taste.\n"
msgstr ""
"这帮人对味道不太挑剔。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/27
msgid ""
"You sound just like Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""
"你跟米勒先生一个腔调。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/29
msgid ""
"When I complained, he simply said, \"As long as it\n"
"gets the job done.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我抱怨的时候，他只说了句：\"能\n"
"管用就行。\"\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/30
msgid ""
"You people are such culinary savages!\n"
msgstr ""
"你们这些烹饪蛮子！\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/31
msgid ""
"Allez tous vous faire voir ! ...Aaaah, somebody take\n"
"me back to Paris! Please!\n"
msgstr ""
"都给我滚开！……啊啊啊，谁来\n"
"把我带回巴黎！求求了！\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/32
msgid ""
"...I think you've had a little too much, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""
"……塞西尔，你喝得有点多了。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/0
msgid ""
"You seem like a very... how do I put this...\n"
"uninhibited woman.\n"
msgstr ""
"你看起来非常……\n"
"怎么说呢……洒脱。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/1
msgid ""
"You think so? I am no different from other Parisian\n"
"women. Not since May 1968.\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？我和巴黎女人没两样。\n"
"1968年五月之后更是如此。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/2
msgid ""
"May 1968... The general strike that almost brought\n"
"down the president?\n"
msgstr ""
"1968年五月……那场差点\n"
"让总统下台的总罢工？\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/3
msgid ""
"Right. But it was more than just a strike.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。但那不只是一场罢工。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/4
msgid ""
"It started with the student movement at\n"
"Strasbourg University in '66.\n"
msgstr ""
"它始于66年\n"
"斯特拉斯堡大学的学生运动。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/5
msgid ""
"They did not want anything from the country, but\n"
"instead sought reform at the school.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们不是向国家索取，\n"
"而是要求学校改革。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/6
msgid ""
"That helped ignite a fire in the hearts of scores of\n"
"dissatisfied young people,\n"
msgstr ""
"这点燃了无数不满的\n"
"年轻人心中之火，\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/7
msgid ""
"and the movement spread all over France.\n"
msgstr ""
"运动随即蔓延到全法国。\n"

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/8
msgid ""
"It was more than just opposition to Vietnam and\n"
"the de Gaulle administration\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/9
msgid ""
"- people also called for free love and the breaking\n"
"away from other old values.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/10
msgid ""
"Looking back, I'm not sure what the main goal\n"
"really was.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/11
msgid ""
"But whatever the case,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/12
msgid ""
"it was more of a young people's movement than a\n"
"strike or a protest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/13
msgid ""
"So... It was like the hippies or something?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/14
msgid ""
"In some ways, perhaps.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/15
msgid ""
"But we weren't blinded by mysticism, nor did we\n"
"seek a return to nature.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/16
msgid ""
"I see. So while they wanted to retreat to their\n"
"closed communes...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/17
msgid ""
"We tried to change the world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/18
msgid ""
"And in doing so we learned that when everyone\n"
"comes together, it can be done.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/19
msgid ""
"You had a lot more success.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/20
msgid ""
"In America hippies have just become a social\n"
"problem,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/21
msgid ""
"while I hear Japan's student movements crashed\n"
"and burned.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/22
msgid ""
"I wonder what was different.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0d60/23
msgid ""
"Good question. I'd like to know myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 459..2020
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/0
msgid ""
"Doc, I'm starting to sense your feelings about\n"
"nukes are a little different from your colleagues.\n"
msgstr ""
"博士，我渐渐感觉到你对核武器的看法\n"
"和你的同事们有点不太一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3009
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/2
msgid ""
"Your little chat with Coldman back there.\n"
msgstr ""
"你刚才和科尔德曼的谈话。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 3023..4472
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/3
msgid ""
"I...told you my father worked on the Manhattan\n"
"Project, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"我……跟你说过我父亲参与过曼哈顿\n"
"计划吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 4625..5015
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/4
msgid ""
"You're familiar with it?\n"
msgstr ""
"你了解它？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 5085..6213
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/5
msgid ""
"The basics, yeah. It was the project that kicked off\n"
"the nuclear age.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道个大概。就是那个开启了\n"
"核时代的计划。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 6227..7300
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/6
msgid ""
"That's right. Some of the finest minds of the 20th\n"
"century,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。20世纪一些最杰出的\n"
"头脑，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 7300..8317
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/7
msgid ""
"including multiple Nobel Prize winners, worked on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"包括多位诺贝尔奖得主，都参与其中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9808
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/8
msgid ""
"They spent over two billion dollars - and that's in\n"
"1940's money.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们花了超二十亿美元，那还是\n"
"40年代的币值。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 9822..11605
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/9
msgid ""
"It culminated in the successful nuclear test at\n"
"Alamogordo on July 16, 1945.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终在1945年7月16日于\n"
"阿拉莫戈多成功进行了核试验。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12566
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/10
msgid ""
"And the first use in combat a few weeks later.\n"
msgstr ""
"几周后首次用于实战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13082
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/11
msgid ""
"Doc?\n"
msgstr ""
"博士？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13096..13444
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/12
msgid ""
"...I can't walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我不能走路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15074
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/13
msgid ""
"My spine isn't shaped like everybody else's. I can't\n"
"move my lower body.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的脊椎和别人的形状不一样。我的下半身\n"
"动不了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 15088..16063
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/14
msgid ""
"So I've never taken a single step, not since I was\n"
"born.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我从出生起，就\n"
"从没迈出过一步。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16077..16983
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/15
msgid ""
"What's that got to do with your dad being in the\n"
"Manhattan Project?\n"
msgstr ""
"这跟你爸参与曼哈顿计划\n"
"有什么关系？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16983..18543
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/16
msgid ""
"As a result of his research, my father was exposed\n"
"to high doses of radiation.\n"
msgstr ""
"由于他的研究，我父亲暴露在\n"
"高剂量辐射之下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 18640..19658
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/17
msgid ""
"It can't be a coincidence that my chromosomes are\n"
"messed up.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的染色体出了问题，这绝不可能是\n"
"巧合。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 19964..20243
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/18
msgid ""
"That's...\n"
msgstr ""
"那是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 20271..21524
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/19
msgid ""
"That's why I didn't want for these nukes to be\n"
"another sword of Damocles.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我不希望核武成为\n"
"另一把达摩克利斯之剑。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 21538..22764
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/20
msgid ""
"I wanted to give them a real purpose: to be a\n"
"deterrent against war.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想赋予它们真正的用途：成为\n"
"威慑战争的力量。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 22778..22987
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/21
msgid ""
"Doc...\n"
msgstr ""
"博士……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 23001..24520
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/22
msgid ""
"And Coldman... We have to stop him. Whatever it\n"
"takes.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有科尔曼……我们必须阻止他。不惜\n"
"一切代价。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 445..2410
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/0
msgid ""
"August 6, 1945 - Hiroshima. August 9 - Nagasaki.\n"
msgstr ""
"1945年8月6日广岛，8月9日长崎。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 2424..3051
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/1
msgid ""
"The atom bomb attacks on Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"对日本的原子弹轰炸。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 3051..3761
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/2
msgid ""
"My father was married to his work.\n"
msgstr ""
"我父亲把一生献给了工作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 3845..5113
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/3
msgid ""
"I don't have a single memory of going places or\n"
"doing stuff with him on weekends.\n"
msgstr ""
"我完全不记得周末\n"
"跟他出去玩过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 5210..6938
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/4
msgid ""
"But even as a kid I knew on some level that it was\n"
"for his family - I respected him.\n"
msgstr ""
"但小时候我就隐约明白\n"
"他是为了家——我尊敬他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 6952..8303
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/5
msgid ""
"My mother used to tell me all the time, \"Your\n"
"father is a brilliant scientist.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲总对我说：\n"
"「你父亲是位杰出的科学家。」\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 8317..9069
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/6
msgid ""
"\"He saved countless American boys from death.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「他让无数美国小伙子免于一死。」\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 9083..9473
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/7
msgid ""
"\"You should be proud of him.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 9473..10546
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/8
msgid ""
"Yeah, you could say the war ended because of\n"
"those bombs...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 10546..12190
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/9
msgid ""
"When I was in the fifth grade, a Japanese student\n"
"transferred to our class.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 12441..13430
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/10
msgid ""
"She showed me photos of Hiroshima after the\n"
"bomb.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 13444..14140
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/11
msgid ""
"I couldn't believe my eyes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 14140..16021
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/12
msgid ""
"A city of over 350,000 people, reduced to a\n"
"scorch mark on the ground.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 16105..16801
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/13
msgid ""
"By a single atomic bomb.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 16829..18181
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/14
msgid ""
"Houses blown off their foundations, burned to\n"
"ashes...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 18264..19449
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/15
msgid ""
"The only things left standing were the skeletons of\n"
"steel-framed buildings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 19449..20034
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/16
msgid ""
"It wasn't just the buildings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 20034..20884
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/17
msgid ""
"Blackened corpses on the side of the road.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 20995..22040
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/18
msgid ""
"Survivors covered head to toe in severe burns...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 22068..23879
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/19
msgid ""
"Within a few months, over 70,000 had died in\n"
"Nagasaki - twice that in Hiroshima.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 23921..24854
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/20
msgid ""
"For years after that I couldn't talk to my father\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 24938..25620
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/21
msgid ""
"- couldn't even stand to look at his face.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 25634..26596
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/22
msgid ""
"I know how you feel, Doc. But your father's your\n"
"father.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 26596..27808
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/23
msgid ""
"If he hadn't worked on that project, my body\n"
"wouldn't be like this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 27850..28518
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/24
msgid ""
"I could be researching something else.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_010_0
#. timeline 28546..29271
#: codec/1/241/0xf1dc0/25
msgid ""
"I could have lived a normal life.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1546
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/0
msgid ""
"It wasn't so long ago the world stood on the brink\n"
"of nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""
"不久前，世界还处在核战争的\n"
"边缘。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 1546..2187
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/1
msgid ""
"Just over on the other side of the Caribbean.\n"
msgstr ""
"就在加勒比的另一边。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3873
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/2
msgid ""
"I was 17 at the time. I'd skipped a few grades and\n"
"was a sophomore at MIT.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时我17岁。跳了几级，\n"
"成了麻省理工二年级学生。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 4026..5126
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/3
msgid ""
"I remember feeling kind of apathetic about the\n"
"news that came in every day.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得自己对每天传来的\n"
"消息感到有些麻木。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6617
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/4
msgid ""
"It seemed clear to me that as long as they had a\n"
"grasp of the concept of nuclear deterrence,\n"
msgstr ""
"在我看来很清楚，只要他们掌握了\n"
"核威慑的概念，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7119
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/5
msgid ""
"there was nothing to fear.\n"
msgstr ""
"就没什么好怕的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 7272..8400
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/6
msgid ""
"Either that, or they were fanning that fear on\n"
"purpose.\n"
msgstr ""
"要么就是他们故意\n"
"煽动那种恐惧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 8400..9947
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/7
msgid ""
"As a way to secure a bigger defense budget...?\n"
"Heh, I can see that.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了确保更大国防预算……？\n"
"呵，我能理解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 9961..10727
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/8
msgid ""
"But if that was their plan, it kind of backfired.\n"
msgstr ""
"但若那是他们计划，反倒弄巧成拙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11856
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/9
msgid ""
"Because it ushered in the era of Détente between\n"
"East and West.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为它开启了东西方之间\n"
"缓和的时代。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 11856..12678
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/10
msgid ""
"Coldman's really going to do it this time.\n"
msgstr ""
"科尔德曼这次真要动手了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13346
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/11
msgid ""
"Once the nuclear genie is out of the bottle,\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦核魔出瓶，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 13346..14182
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/12
msgid ""
"the yoke of deterrence is going to be meaningless.\n"
msgstr ""
"威慑的枷锁就毫无意义了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15116
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/13
msgid ""
"People will die. Cities will burn.\n"
msgstr ""
"人们会死。城市会燃烧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 15116..16161
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/14
msgid ""
"We have to stop him now, before it's too late to\n"
"turn back.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们必须现在就阻止他，趁还来得及\n"
"回头。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/0
msgid ""
"So you've been doing nuclear research your whole\n"
"life?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你一辈子\n"
"都在做核研究？\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/1
msgid ""
"No, not really. At first I wanted to be an aerospace\n"
"engineer.\n"
msgstr ""
"也不全是。起初我想当\n"
"航空航天工程师。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/2
msgid ""
"For me, the Sputnik launch was a good shock, not\n"
"a bad one.\n"
msgstr ""
"对我来说，斯普特尼克发射\n"
"是惊喜而非打击。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/3
msgid ""
"I thought the age when science was used for war\n"
"was over,\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为科学用于战争的时代\n"
"已经结束，\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/4
msgid ""
"and that a glorious age of space exploration was\n"
"dawning.\n"
msgstr ""
"太空探索的辉煌时代\n"
"即将到来。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/5
msgid ""
"The year I skipped ahead and got into MIT,\n"
msgstr ""
"我跳级考进麻省理工那一年，\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/6
msgid ""
"Gagarin went into orbit, which made me more\n"
"excited than ever.\n"
msgstr ""
"加加林进入太空轨道，\n"
"让我无比兴奋。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/7
msgid ""
"Of course, even back then,\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，即便那时，\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/8
msgid ""
"I knew the space race was just another facet of\n"
"the Cold War...\n"
msgstr ""
"我也知道太空竞赛\n"
"只是冷战的另一面……\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/9
msgid ""
"Moscow had a leg up on us, and we were\n"
"desperate to catch up.\n"
msgstr ""
"莫斯科领先我们一步，\n"
"我们拼命追赶。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/10
msgid ""
"I know. But for me it was a happy time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。但那段时间我很快乐。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/11
msgid ""
"I joined NASA - got to do the kind of research I\n"
"loved.\n"
msgstr ""
"我进了NASA，\n"
"能做自己喜欢的研究。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/12
msgid ""
"Our nation's prestige hinged on our work.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家的声望系于我们的工作。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/13
msgid ""
"They gave us whatever resources we asked for.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们要什么资源他们就给什么。\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/14
msgid ""
"I knew you could turn a rocket into an ICBM by\n"
"fitting it with a nuclear warhead,\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道火箭装上核弹头\n"
"就能变成洲际导弹，\n"

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/15
msgid ""
"but that didn't bother me so much.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/16
msgid ""
"It didn't last long, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/17
msgid ""
"The space and nuclear arms races took up\n"
"enormous sums of money.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/18
msgid ""
"America beat Russia to the moon, but that's where\n"
"it ended.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/19
msgid ""
"Then came Détente.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/20
msgid ""
"Exactly. NASA's budget was slashed as a result.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/21
msgid ""
"My father being a nuclear expert and all,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/22
msgid ""
"they put me to work on a more obvious deterrent:\n"
"missiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/23
msgid ""
"At NASA, I'd been researching a locomotion system\n"
"for lunar exploration.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/24
msgid ""
"Tires aren't suited to driving around on the moon,\n"
"you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/25
msgid ""
"And that's how I caught Coldman's eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/0
msgid ""
"But you know... there's something I've never been\n"
"able to figure out.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你知道……有件事我一直\n"
"想不明白。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/1
msgid ""
"Is the Cold War really a war, or is it really peace...?\n"
msgstr ""
"冷战究竟是战争，还是和平……？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/2
msgid ""
"Doc, what are you...?\n"
msgstr ""
"博士，你在……？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/3
msgid ""
"People called it a \"cold war,\" but I disagreed.\n"
msgstr ""
"人们称之为\"冷战\"，但我不同意。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/4
msgid ""
"Sure, nuclear stockpiles are increasing, threats are\n"
"multiplying,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，核武库在增加，威胁在\n"
"倍增，\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/5
msgid ""
"the U.S. and the Soviet Union have enough power\n"
msgstr ""
"美苏两国的力量足以\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/6
msgid ""
"to destroy the human race a hundred times over.\n"
msgstr ""
"毁灭人类上百次。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/7
msgid ""
"But nobody's actually being killed. Small-scale\n"
"conflicts and proxy wars, maybe...\n"
msgstr ""
"但实际没人被杀。小规模\n"
"冲突和代理人战争，也许……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/8
msgid ""
"But nuclear deterrence has averted another world\n"
"war.\n"
msgstr ""
"但核威慑避免了另一场世界\n"
"大战。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/9
msgid ""
"The world's far more peaceful today than it was\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""
"如今的世界比以往\n"
"和平得多。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/10
msgid ""
"And the breakthroughs we've made in space\n"
"exploration\n"
msgstr ""
"还有我们在太空探索方面\n"
"取得的突破\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/11
msgid ""
"thanks to Cold War competition - fantastic, don't\n"
"you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"多亏冷战竞争——太棒了，你不\n"
"觉得吗？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/12
msgid ""
"No... We didn't need to rush into space like that...\n"
msgstr ""
"不……我们不该那样急着进太空……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/13
msgid ""
"Going into space may have been mankind's dream,\n"
msgstr ""
"进入太空也许是人类的梦想，\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/14
msgid ""
"but good people were sacrificed in the scramble.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在这场争夺中好人被牺牲了。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/15
msgid ""
"...Maybe so. NASA's definitely got some skeletons in\n"
"its closet...\n"
msgstr ""
"……也许吧。NASA确实有些见不得\n"
"人的秘密……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/16
msgid ""
"Same goes for the nuclear arms race.\n"
msgstr ""
"核军备竞赛也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/17
msgid ""
"Atomic testing has killed civilians and exposed\n"
"thousands to radiation.\n"
msgstr ""
"核试验害死了平民，让数千人\n"
"暴露在辐射中。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/18
msgid ""
"Believe me, I know...\n"
msgstr ""
"相信我，我知道……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/19
msgid ""
"And now this... What peace was I trying to protect,\n"
"anyway?\n"
msgstr ""
"而现在这个……我到底是想守护怎样的和平，\n"
"话说回来？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/20
msgid ""
"The more I think about it, the less I understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"越想越不明白。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/0
msgid ""
"Let's speak in hypotheticals for a minute.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们先做个假设。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/1
msgid ""
"Say you wanted to make a clone of yourself...\n"
msgstr ""
"假设你想克隆一个自己……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/2
msgid ""
"A clone? Para-Medic had the same idea. It's\n"
"science fiction.\n"
msgstr ""
"克隆？军医也这么想过。\n"
"那是科幻小说。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/3
msgid ""
"I'm just hypothesizing here. OK, not a clone, then.\n"
"You have any kids?\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是假设。那不说克隆。\n"
"你有孩子吗？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/4
msgid ""
"Nope.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/5
msgid ""
"Wife?\n"
msgstr ""
"妻子呢？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/6
msgid ""
"...Never been tied down.\n"
msgstr ""
"……从没被束缚过。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/7
msgid ""
"OK, then... so we're still talking hypotheticals.\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧……那还是假设。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/8
msgid ""
"Say you had a son who'd inherited your genes,\n"
msgstr ""
"假设你有个继承了你基因的儿子，\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/9
msgid ""
"someone with the same combat abilities as you.\n"
msgstr ""
"拥有和你一样的战斗能力。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/10
msgid ""
"Would you challenge him to a fight?\n"
msgstr ""
"你会向他挑战吗？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/11
msgid ""
"...Hmm. Not to sound cocky, but I wouldn't want to\n"
"do that. No telling who'd survive.\n"
msgstr ""
"……嗯。不是我自大，\n"
"但我不想，谁能活下来还真不好说。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/12
msgid ""
"I'll bet. You picked up on the Pupa-5000's combat\n"
"patterns in seconds.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是。你几秒钟就摸清了\n"
"Pupa-5000的战斗模式。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/13
msgid ""
"Only with your advice, Doc.\n"
msgstr ""
"全靠你的指点，博士。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/14
msgid ""
"If anybody could learn to do it just by listening, it'd\n"
"be easy.\n"
msgstr ""
"要是光听就能学会，\n"
"那谁都办得到。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/15
msgid ""
"But you - you're a born soldier.\n"
msgstr ""
"可你是天生的战士。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/16
msgid ""
"Yeah. You must have been born with genes geared\n"
"for combat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/17
msgid ""
"Soldier genes, if you will.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/18
msgid ""
"...Genes geared for combat? I don't care how\n"
"advanced their research is.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/19
msgid ""
"You can't blame genes for everything.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/20
msgid ""
"Blame genes...? You think it's funny.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/21
msgid ""
"...What?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/22
msgid ""
"You think genes have nothing to do with this body\n"
"I was born with?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/23
msgid ""
"I... I don't know...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/24
msgid ""
"...Look, that fear of facing someone of equal ability\n"
"in combat...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/25
msgid ""
"Imagine that on a strategic scale. That's the\n"
"concept of nuclear deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/26
msgid ""
"The idea is, when all sides are armed with the\n"
"destructive power of nuclear weapons,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/27
msgid ""
"they'll avoid nuclear war in order to prevent mutual\n"
"annihilation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/28
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound all that sophisticated to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/29
msgid ""
"Exactly! It's so simple in principle. But because it's\n"
"so simple,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/30
msgid ""
"whether or not it works properly depends on the\n"
"people involved.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/31
msgid ""
"In that sense, what we're looking at now is a\n"
"malfunction in deterrence theory.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/32
msgid ""
"Coldman...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/33
msgid ""
"You got it. Please, Snake, don't let deterrence die.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/0
msgid ""
"Nuclear deterrence means preventing the use of\n"
"nuclear weapons\n"
msgstr ""
"核威慑意味着防止在\n"
"国家间冲突中使用核武器\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 1421..2661
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/1
msgid ""
"in conflicts between states. But what about other\n"
"situations?\n"
msgstr ""
"在国家间的冲突中。但其他\n"
"情况又如何呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 2953..3761
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/3
msgid ""
"Terrorism has been on the rise in recent years,\n"
msgstr ""
"近年来恐怖主义不断抬头，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 3761..4736
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/4
msgid ""
"from separatist movements to far-left extremists.\n"
msgstr ""
"从分离主义运动到极左极端分子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 4736..6018
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/5
msgid ""
"What would happen if nuclear weapons fell into\n"
"terrorist hands?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果核武器落入恐怖分子手中\n"
"会怎样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 6018..7091
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/6
msgid ""
"Without a state - that is, without territory of their\n"
"own\n"
msgstr ""
"没有国家，即没有自己的\n"
"领土\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 7091..8080
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/7
msgid ""
"- the chances of having nukes used against them\n"
"are slim.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 他们遭核武打击的可能性\n"
"微乎其微。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 8122..8958
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/8
msgid ""
"They have no reason to fear a nuclear strike.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们没理由害怕核打击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 9000..10476
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/9
msgid ""
"Conversely, they have no reason to hesitate to use\n"
"nukes against their adversaries.\n"
msgstr ""
"反过来，他们也没理由犹豫\n"
"对敌动用核武。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 10476..11633
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/10
msgid ""
"You've got a point. All the ICBMs and strategic\n"
"bombers in the world\n"
msgstr ""
"有道理。世上所有洲际导弹和战略\n"
"轰炸机\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/11
msgid ""
"amount to nothing against a terrorist group.\n"
msgstr ""
"对恐怖组织都毫无用处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 12260..13318
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/12
msgid ""
"Right! Of course, this is all still hypothetical.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错！当然，这些都还只是假设。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13360..13959
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/13
msgid ""
"Countries keep their nukes under tight watch\n"
msgstr ""
"各国对核武看管严密\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13959..15032
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/14
msgid ""
"- there's no immediate danger of terrorists getting\n"
"their hands on them.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 目前不存在恐怖分子\n"
"获得这些武器的直接危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 15032..16021
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/15
msgid ""
"But the day may come when the proposition of\n"
"nuclear terrorism\n"
msgstr ""
"但总有一天，核恐怖主义\n"
"可能成真\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16021..16885
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/16
msgid ""
"makes nuclear deterrence theory a dead letter.\n"
msgstr ""
"会让核威慑理论彻底失效。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16885..18125
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/17
msgid ""
"Nuclear terrorism... Interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"核恐怖主义……有意思。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/0
msgid ""
"What are we going to do, Snake? If Peace Walker\n"
"attacks Mother Base...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们该怎么办，Snake？\n"
"要是和平行者袭击母基地……\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/1
msgid ""
"Relax. We've got the entire MSF out to make sure\n"
"that doesn't happen.\n"
msgstr ""
"放心。全体MSF都在行动，\n"
"不会让那种事发生。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, but... Peace Walker's missiles have\n"
"one-megaton warheads.\n"
msgstr ""
"话是这么说……和平行者的导弹\n"
"装的是百万吨级弹头。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/3
msgid ""
"The fireball alone'd be a mile in diameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"光是火球直径就有一英里。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/4
msgid ""
"Everything in the vicinity of ground zero will be\n"
"vaporized by the heat rays.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆心附近的一切\n"
"都会被热辐射气化。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/5
msgid ""
"Then there's the blast, which travels at hundreds\n"
"of miles per hour.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/6
msgid ""
"And the fires. And the...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/7
msgid ""
"The huge dose of radiation from the initial nuclear\n"
"reaction.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/8
msgid ""
"That too. There won't be a single survivor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm aware of that. Look, Doc, you made that\n"
"thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/10
msgid ""
"You know better than anybody what it's capable of.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/11
msgid ""
"Right now you've got to give me a rational,\n"
"scientific estimate of the damage.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/12
msgid ""
"If we're talking about a nuclear explosion, it's more\n"
"that just MSF's problem.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/13
msgid ""
"You're right Snake, sorry about that...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/14
msgid ""
"Like I was saying, Mother Base would be wiped out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/15
msgid ""
"Any ships in the area could be caught in the blast,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/16
msgid ""
"We'd need to send out a warning.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/17
msgid ""
"The thing to worry about most is the fallout.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/18
msgid ""
"The dust of death...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/19
msgid ""
"If it goes off over water,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/20
msgid ""
"the particles will be smaller than with an explosion\n"
"over land,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/21
msgid ""
"so the wind will scatter the fallout over a wider\n"
"area.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/22
msgid ""
"Clouds will form around the salt crystals in the\n"
"seawater,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/23
msgid ""
"causing contaminated rain to fall downwind.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/24
msgid ""
"Yeah, got a taste of that myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/25
msgid ""
"On Bikini Atoll?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/26
msgid ""
"That's right, the 1954 Castle Bravo test created\n"
"fallout 300 miles downwind.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/27
msgid ""
"Poisoned a lot of local residents and ships, so I\n"
"hear.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/28
msgid ""
"The yield of Peace Walker's warheads isn't that big,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/29
msgid ""
"but the amount of fallout will largely depend on\n"
"weather conditions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/30
msgid ""
"It's impossible to make a quick and easy estimate.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/31
msgid ""
"...If it gets into the trade winds, it could come\n"
"straight to Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/32
msgid ""
"What was it Coldman was saying? About leaving\n"
"people \"free to help out\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/33
msgid ""
"He's out of his mind. What does he think's going to\n"
"happen?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/34
msgid ""
"When they get hit by rain containing high\n"
"concentrations of fallout,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/35
msgid ""
"a lot of them will die from the external exposure\n"
"alone.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/36
msgid ""
"The rain will seep into the ground, contaminating\n"
"the water supply and crops.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/37
msgid ""
"When they ingest the stuff, the internal exposure\n"
"starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/38
msgid ""
"Strontium-90 and cesium-137 have half-lives of\n"
"around 30 years\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/39
msgid ""
"- the effects stay with you your entire life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/40
msgid ""
"Leukemia, cataracts, dermatitis, cancer... And it\n"
"affects reproduction, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/41
msgid ""
"...I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/42
msgid ""
"Even today, 30 years after World War II,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/43
msgid ""
"thousands of people still suffer from exposure to\n"
"the bomb.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/44
msgid ""
"We can't let Coldman create more of them just to\n"
"prove his point.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/45
msgid ""
"...I know it sounds crazy,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/46
msgid ""
"but I created Peace Walker so that that kind of\n"
"thing would never happen again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/47
msgid ""
"Don't worry, Doc. We'll stop it, one way or another.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 445..1880
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/0
msgid ""
"I gotta say... I'm surprised you helped us arm Metal\n"
"Gear with Nukes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我得说……你居然帮我们\n"
"给Metal Gear装上核弹。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 1880..2131
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/1
msgid ""
"What of it?\n"
msgstr ""
"那又怎样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 2131..3538
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/2
msgid ""
"Don't get me wrong, I'm grateful and all, but... you\n"
"sure about this?\n"
msgstr ""
"别误会，我很感激，可是……\n"
"你真想好了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 3594..4973
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/3
msgid ""
"They may be for MSF's self-defense, but they're\n"
"still nukes.\n"
msgstr ""
"就算是为了MSF自卫，\n"
"那终究是核武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 5001..6046
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/4
msgid ""
"It's essentially the same thing as Peace Walker,\n"
"which you despised.\n"
msgstr ""
"这和你厌恶的和平行者\n"
"本质上没两样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 6046..6645
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/5
msgid ""
"...See, that's exactly it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 6645..6924
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/6
msgid ""
"What is?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 6938..8010
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/7
msgid ""
"You don't hide your motives. You tell the truth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 8094..9027
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/8
msgid ""
"That's what makes you different from those CIA\n"
"bastards.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 9027..9752
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/9
msgid ""
"They lay on the charm - win you over.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 9780..10741
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/10
msgid ""
"And then, when things get hairy, they turn their\n"
"backs on you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11368
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/11
msgid ""
"...I'm just telling it like it is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 11368..12622
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/12
msgid ""
"Which is why I get the feeling that you wouldn't be\n"
"stupid enough to use them...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 12845..13890
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/13
msgid ""
"OK, I'll come out and say it. I trust you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 13890..14336
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/14
msgid ""
"You give me too much credit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 14837..16230
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/16
msgid ""
"Besides, there's more uses for bipedal locomotion\n"
"technology than weapons.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 16258..17846
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/17
msgid ""
"We make it small enough, and it could have\n"
"applications in robotics and prosthetic limbs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 17930..18710
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/18
msgid ""
"Maybe one day I'll even be able to walk.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 19017..19323
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/19
msgid ""
"Nice thought.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 19323..20591
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/20
msgid ""
"I wanna stand on my own feet, be master of my\n"
"own fate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 20619..22054
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/21
msgid ""
"And I'll use your strength to help me do it... if you\n"
"don't mind, of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 22054..22834
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/22
msgid ""
"Nah, it's a fair enough deal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 22876..23141
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/23
msgid ""
"Thanks.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 23141..24185
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/24
msgid ""
"People can change, I know... but I trust you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0180_000_0
#. timeline 24255..25133
#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/25
msgid ""
"I trust you to be the guy I know now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..2340
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/0
msgid ""
"The aim of the Peace Walker Project is to achieve\n"
"robust nuclear deterrence across Central America\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者计划的目标是在中美洲全境\n"
"实现强力核威慑\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3538
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/1
msgid ""
"by deploying a new nuclear weapon system along\n"
"the Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"方式是在加勒比沿岸部署\n"
"新型核武器系统。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4430
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/2
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is also the name of the system itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者也是这套系统本身的名称。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 4639..6213
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/3
msgid ""
"A nuclear weapon named \"Peace\"... I can just see\n"
"the look on Kaz's face.\n"
msgstr ""
"名为“和平”的核武……我能想象\n"
"卡兹的表情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7300
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/4
msgid ""
"So why exactly does this new system need legs in\n"
"the first place?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，这个新系统究竟为什么\n"
"首先需要腿呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7300..7704
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/5
msgid ""
"Because it's a \"Walker.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"因为它是“行者”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7704..8094
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/6
msgid ""
"An unmanned weapon\n"
msgstr ""
"无人武器\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 8094..9613
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/7
msgid ""
"moving under its own power and capable of\n"
"launching a deterrent strike from anywhere...\n"
msgstr ""
"自行移动，能从任何地方\n"
"发动威慑打击……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 9738..10671
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/8
msgid ""
"That's the whole idea behind Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是和平行者的全部构想。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/0
msgid ""
"The reason Peace Walker is a mobile nuclear\n"
"weapons system\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者之所以是移动式核\n"
"武器系统\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2452
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/1
msgid ""
"is to maximize its potential as a nuclear deterrent.\n"
msgstr ""
"是为了最大化其核威慑潜力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 2730..3873
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/3
msgid ""
"If need be, Peace Walker can stay constantly on\n"
"the move\n"
msgstr ""
"必要时，和平行者可以不停\n"
"移动\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 3873..4764
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/4
msgid ""
"so that the adversary can't pinpoint its position...\n"
msgstr ""
"让敌人无法锁定其位置……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5684
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/5
msgid ""
"That allows it to avoid preemptive enemy strikes.\n"
msgstr ""
"从而避免遭敌方先发制人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 5684..6645
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/6
msgid ""
"So you're saying it keeps the retaliation card in\n"
"play.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你是说它会保留报复卡在\n"
"手牌中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 6645..7397
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/7
msgid ""
"Coldman likes to brag about it in this way...\n"
msgstr ""
"科尔德曼就爱这么吹嘘……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8219
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/8
msgid ""
"Like a land-based version of an SSBN.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像陆基版的战略核潜艇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9013
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/9
msgid ""
"And there's another reason for them to be mobile.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们能移动还有另一个原因。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10184
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/10
msgid ""
"Peace Walker also has a self-destruct function.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者还有自毁功能。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 445..1351
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/0
msgid ""
"Why would Peace Walker need a self-destruct\n"
"function?\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者为什么需要\n"
"自毁功能？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 1351..2493
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/1
msgid ""
"You saw it, didn't you, Snake? That sphere on\n"
"Peace Walker's head?\n"
msgstr ""
"你看到了吧，Snake？\n"
"和平行者头部那个球体？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 2702..3287
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/3
msgid ""
"That's a hydrogen bomb.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是氢弹。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 3287..4569
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/4
msgid ""
"What?! You're telling me that thing's a\n"
"thermonuclear device?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？！你是说那玩意\n"
"是热核装置？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 4569..5461
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/5
msgid ""
"Do they have any idea what kind of destruction\n"
"that thing would cause...?\n"
msgstr ""
"他们知道那东西\n"
"会造成多大的破坏吗……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 5475..7049
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/6
msgid ""
"I know, it's crazy. I mean, even overkill has its\n"
"limits.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道，太疯狂了。\n"
"就算是过度杀伤也该有个限度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 7077..8164
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/7
msgid ""
"If it's strategic value they want, they could have\n"
"gone with something smaller.\n"
msgstr ""
"要的是战略价值的话，\n"
"完全可以做得更小。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 8178..9473
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/8
msgid ""
"It's like they want a weapon on par with Russia's\n"
"Tsar Bomba.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 9473..10295
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/9
msgid ""
"This arms race is running way out of control.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 10295..11466
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/10
msgid ""
"It's an evolutionary dead-end... A saber-toothed\n"
"tiger.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 11466..12510
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/11
msgid ""
"You can't load a warhead that big on a missile, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 12524..13931
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/12
msgid ""
"And no strategic bomber could carry it. That's\n"
"where Peace Walker comes in.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_010_0
#. timeline 13931..15840
#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/13
msgid ""
"So it waltzes into enemy territory carrying a\n"
"hydrogen bomb and blows itself up. Christ.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 459..2145
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/0
msgid ""
"The biggest nuclear warhead ever actually\n"
"detonated was the Soviet RDS-220,\n"
msgstr ""
"实际引爆过最大的核弹头\n"
"是苏联RDS-220，\n"
